        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let the side lengths be $x$ cm and $y$ cm.\n$$\\begin{align*}2(x+y)&=13\\\\x+y&=\\frac{13}{2}\\\\xy&=10\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute $y=\\frac{13}{2}-x$ into the area equation.\n$$\\begin{align*}x\\left(\\frac{13}{2}-x\\right)&=10\\\\2x^2-13x+20&=0\\\\(2x-5)(x-4)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x=\\frac52$ or $x=4$, with the other side $4$ or $\\frac52$ respectively. The dimensions are $4\\text{ cm}\\times\\frac52\\text{ cm}$.\n\nCheck: $4\\times\\frac52=10$ and $2\\left(4+\\frac52\\right)=13$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
